gBn(){return"Management should be individualized based on disease type, extent, patient age, prior treatments, and predominant symptom."},
gvj(){return"In clinical practice, management is usually divided into pain-related or infertility-related approaches, as treatment strategies may differ or even be opposite."},
gBh(){return"In asymptomatic patients, expectant management is often appropriate if no risk factors or concerning findings are present."},
gBg(){return"Surgery in asymptomatic patients should be individualized and not based solely on the presence of endometriosis."},
gBr(){return"For pain associated with endometriosis, the main options are medical treatment and surgery."},
gBq(){return"Medical treatment aims to reduce inflammation and suppress endometriotic lesions. It includes NSAIDs and hormonal therapies, especially progestins such as dienogest."},
gBs(){return"Surgery should effectively treat lesions while preserving ovarian function and fertility."},
gBm(){return"In symptomatic endometrioma, medical treatment should not be considered definitive management of the cyst."},
gBl(){return"Surgical management depends on size, ovarian reserve, age, and reproductive goals. Cystectomy is standard, though conservative approaches may be used in selected cases."},
gvi(){return"In large or recurrent endometriomas, preservation of ovarian reserve is critical."},
gBk(){return"Deep endometriosis with pain requires individualized management based on symptoms, location, severity, and reproductive goals."},
gBi(){return"Medical therapy may be considered initially, but surgery may be required for persistent pain, anatomical involvement, or treatment failure."},
gBj(){return"Deep endometriosis often requires a multidisciplinary surgical approach."},
gBp(){return"In endometriosis-associated infertility, the main options are surgery and assisted reproductive technologies."},
gBo(){return"In infertility with endometrioma, management must be individualized."},
gvk(){return"Medical therapy does not improve fertility. Management depends on age, ovarian reserve, prior surgeries, tubal status, male factor, and EFI prognosis."},
gvl(){return"Medical therapy has no role in treating infertility associated with endometriosis."},
